  "question": "Can Google Books public surfaces for the exact 1997 《北京图书馆馆史资料汇编（二）：1949—1966》 directly recover or reliably page-locate pp.446—449, or bind target 3482/3483, without guessing object IDs/endpoints or overreading search-index hits?",
  "answer": "No. The exact bibliographic object BZ0M0gEACAAJ confirms the 1997 ISBN/title/1811-page identity but emits no usable in-book q= contract; its source-emitted html_text route returns HTTP 403. It does source-emit alternate object RuGEAAAAIAAJ. That alternate independently preserves the same bibliographic identity and does emit in-book q= links, so targeted searches are authorized. However the resulting snippets expose no usable printed page numbers for pp.446—449 and do not directly recover those pages. Searches for target titles and 3482/3483/03482/03483 yield no direct target snippet, but those zero results have no full-text absence authority. Critically, apparently positive searches are demonstrably unsafe: 瞿氏 returns a 1932 瞿兑之 deposit passage unrelated to Tieqin Tongjian Lou, 赵万里 returns a staff chronology passage, the query 这些善本入藏本馆 is tokenized into unrelated 善本/入藏 snippets rather than the literal phrase, and 可为全国之冠 returns a general library-takeover statement rather than the NLC-2024 Tieqin intake quotation. Therefore Google Books currently supplies a searchable-index boundary and false-positive classifier, not direct pp.446—449 collation or item-level acquisition evidence.",
